# Paths excluded from the coverage gate (regex over coverage-profile lines).
# Keep this list small and well-justified.

# Entry point — wiring, flag parsing, signal handling, no behaviour worth a test.
github.com/kfet/harb/cmd/harb/main.go

# Frontend static-check helper — invoked via `make lint-frontend`,
# not exercised by go test.
github.com/kfet/harb/scripts/lintfrontend/main.go

# End-to-end test package; exercised by `make e2e`, not unit tests.
^github.com/kfet/harb/e2e/

# Reeder / GReader conformance suite — embedder-driven contract tests
# whose code is mostly assertion plumbing (t.Fatal branches on JSON
# unmarshal etc). The behaviour each contract pins is exercised in the
# packages it drives; the suite itself is test-support code.
^github.com/kfet/harb/internal/reedercompat/

# Self-update: deep filesystem I/O error branches (chmod after create,
# rename atop running exe, io.Copy mid-stream, tar.Next post-header).
# Happy path + all classified errors (network, checksum, missing entry,
# bad gzip, managed paths) are covered; contriving the remaining
# kernel-level errors adds noise without informing the behaviour.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/selfupdate/selfupdate.go

# Store Open folds logs immediately after migrateStateLog has opened/scanned
# the same files; these error returns are only reachable by a filesystem race
# between migration and folding. The direct foldLog error path is exercised.
# buildIndex's top-level ReadDir error is similarly race-only (entries/
# was just walked by migrateEntryHashes).
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/store.go:131\.71,133\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/store.go:134\.74,136\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/store.go:138\.39,140\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/store.go:153\.3,153\.13
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/store.go:244\.3,244\.13

# FileOPML lazy init uses double-checked locking. The second nil-check
# inside the write-locked section is the race-loser branch — only
# reachable when two goroutines call Load concurrently on a fresh
# FileOPML and one wins the upgrade. Behaviour-equivalent to the
# winner's path; not worth a deterministic-race test rig.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/config/config.go:105\.18,107\.3

# Passkey: defensive error returns unreachable in practice.
# - newHandle: crypto/rand.Read failing.
# - Begin{Registration,Login}: json.Marshal of a fixed map of only
#   strings/ints/slices/nested maps never errors.
# - CredentialStore.persistLocked: json.MarshalIndent of the credential
#   set (string + []byte + time fields) never errors.
# Every real error path (verification, decode, persist-mkdir, redeem,
# expiry, duplicate) is exercised.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/passkey/passkey.go:104\.40,106\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/passkey/passkey.go:192\.16,194\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/passkey/passkey.go:272\.16,274\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/passkey/credstore.go:151\.16,153\.3

# UI passkey handlers: defensive branches unreachable in practice.
# - register/login Begin error returns: Begin* only fails on crypto/rand
#   or json.Marshal of a fixed map (both covignored in internal/passkey).
# - mustJSON's panic: only fixed server-controlled maps are passed.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/ui/passkey.go:74\.16,77\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/ui/passkey.go:109\.16,112\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/ui/passkey.go:166\.16,167\.40

# Reader ETag helpers: opmlFingerprint degrades to an empty string on
# OPML.Marshal failure, which is a defensive return for an encoding bug
# that doesn't happen in practice (Marshal only manipulates strings and
# already-validated structs). etagOPML / etagOPMLState then return ""
# so the handler skips ETag handling and serves a normal 200 — i.e. the
# fallback is a correctness no-op, not a behaviour to assert. applyETag
# has the same degrade-to-no-op branch on empty etag.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/reader/reader.go:994\.16,998\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/reader/reader.go:1007\.14,1009\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/reader/reader.go:1019\.14,1021\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/reader/reader.go:1031\.16,1033\.3

# webflow-to-feed: goquery.NewDocumentFromReader only errors when the
# underlying io.Reader errors. The body is always wrapped in a
# strings.Reader (in-memory, never errors) and html.Parse itself does not
# return parse errors on malformed markup, so this defensive
# leave-the-body-for-the-next-stage branch is unreachable in practice.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/poll/resolve/webflow.go:146\.16,148\.3

# content enrichment: largestRichText / extractArticle wrap the fetched
# body in an in-memory bytes.Reader, and isLinkOnlyHTML / hasAnchor wrap
# their input in a strings.Reader, so goquery.NewDocumentFromReader cannot
# error (the reader never errors and html.Parse does not reject malformed
# HTML). Same unreachable defensive branch as the resolver above.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/poll/enrich.go:195\.16,197\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/poll/enrich.go:212\.16,214\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/poll/enrich.go:297\.16,299\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/poll/enrich.go:105\.16,107\.3

# Sticky-identity migration (idmigrate.go) + sticky sidecar (store.go):
# defensive error returns and by-construction invariants. Every reachable
# behaviour (seeding, collapse, in-place OR-preserving state remap, dry-run,
# version-gate skip, idempotence, corrupt-sidecar / malformed-ndjson /
# unreadable-dir / read-only-apply faults) is exercised; what remains is:
# - identityMarkerPresent's non-ErrNotExist os.Stat error (125-127, 515): a
#   filesystem race; both the present and ErrNotExist arms ARE tested.
# - Accounting-invariant abort (245-248): survivor_count = old − collapses holds
#   by construction (survivors is the distinct-newHash set); guard cannot fire.
# - assertStatePreserved error propagation (257-262) and its "no survivor" arm
#   (498-500): every remap value is a survivor newHash by construction, so the
#   error is unreachable; the happy path + orphan-hash skip ARE tested.
# - Apply-phase saveStickyGUIDs / read.log remap error arms (277-279, 285-290):
#   mid-apply I/O failures after applyFileRewrites already succeeded;
#   applyFileRewrites' own failure IS tested (read-only feed dir).
# - jsonMarshal(Entry) in applyFileRewrites (354-356) and the marker marshal
#   (525-527): encoding a fixed struct of strings/times/slices never errors
#   (same class as the existing passkey/reader marshal covignores).
# - gatherFeedEntries ErrNotExist arm (391-393): feedHashDirs only yields dirs
#   that exist; the read-error arm IS tested.
# - remapStateLog non-ErrNotExist open error (560) and scanner error (590-595):
#   the ErrNotExist arm + happy/drop paths ARE tested; these are the same
#   defensive I/O branches as the covered migrateStateLog equivalents.
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/idmigrate.go:125\.58,127\.4
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/idmigrate.go:246\.86,249\.3
github.com/kfet/harb/internal/store/idmigrate.go:258\.83,260\.3
